# Actual finite forest admission resource observations

This fixed developer job observes the public `admit_packages` API, independently of library publication. The library qualification has 37 cases: 26 existing layout/admission and 11 new forest cases, plus fmt/Clippy/WASM. Those case counts are not a feature-acceptance count.

Ten size/topology groups retain two warmups and seven measured fresh-process samples each: 90 observations, ten pre-cancellation and five invalid-CLI controls. Default 32/64/128 flat/star inputs admit; 256/1024 refuse Work. Refusal latency is not successful capacity. Requested allocator traffic, retained live heap, phase peak, logical allowance and process VmHWM remain distinct. There is no p95 claim.

The raw source/tool/library/binary bindings, all streams, observer inputs, invocation proof, actual resource controls, Samsung receipt and absent cleanup observation are retained. `evidence/input-recovery.json` resolves every recorded phase to checked local bytes or exact immutable #183/#184 Git blobs. `evidence/dependencies.json` names those immutable commits and seals. The earlier pre-format profiler epoch remains historical data.

The five active job sources are exact copies of the executed sources. Their fixed original paths, including the shared helper locator, are provenance; reproduction requires a newly reviewed fresh output/path epoch. The data-only assembler is retained and counted. Independent packet review remains required before publication.

Placement/continuation, real callers, native/UI/worker behavior and successful capacity acceptance remain OPEN. Shared ownership-helper qualification is reused at its exact #184 bytes; this packet does not introduce another cleanup algorithm.
